  "why": "Stopped by Brilliant Nodes after step 26. The Examplecoin mining check had no majority on two attempts (two validators timed out on the first; on the second the leader's model read explorer B's pool table as showing nothing, and two validators disagreed); the run stopped there and was resumed about six minutes later. Steps run on resume re-read the views of cases A and B after their bonds had already been decided, so those two reads show UPHELD and RELEASED where BONDED was expected. The re-check of case C (Turncoin) then had no majority (0 of 5 matching the leader, 363 s), and its 600-second re-check window, and case D's, closed before either could be sent again. Cases C and D therefore could not show the overturn and the disagreement on this deployment.",
